## Regression Diagnostics

With multiple regression, we want to check on...

- Normality of residuals

  + Relationships with other variables

- Multicollinearity among predictors

- Outliers


# Residuals

## Residuals

We want to see that our residuals are **normally distributed** and have constant variance across all levels of the predictors.

Can extract residuals from a model with `resid(lm_model)` or `residuals(lm_model)`.

:::: {.columns}
::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
residuals(m3) |>
  head()
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
         1          2          3          4          5          6 
 538.38213  361.43569 -656.34648 -366.88988  -52.96734  432.25908 
```


:::
:::


:::

::: {.column width="50%"}

::: {.panel-tabset}
### Plot

::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![](lab_13_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-7-1.svg){fig-align='center' width=480}
:::
:::


### Code

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
penguins_cleaned |>
  add_column(residuals = residuals(m3)) |>
  ggplot(aes(x = bill_length_mm, y = residuals)) +
  geom_density() +
  theme_classic()
```
:::

:::


:::
::::


## Residuals

We want to see that our residuals are normally distributed and have **constant variance across all levels of the predictors**.

Can extract residuals from a model with `resid(lm_model)` or `residuals(lm_model)`.

